        "original_id": "6fe448a8-8ad0-51e0-8610-08c5419ebb6b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kang Sung-yeon, Jang Hyuk, Han Ye-seul, Kim Min-joon, Son Hyun-joo, Kim Kap-soo\n- Works: King and the Clown, Tazza\n- Roles: Jang Nok-su, Prince Yeonsan's concubine\n- Companies: Cinema Service, CJ Entertainment\n- Topics: South Korean film, South Korean television\n\nFacts:\n- On 29 December 2005, King and the Clown was released.\n- King and the Clown has a runtime of 119 minutes.\n- Cinema Service distributed King and the Clown domestically, and CJ Entertainment distributed it internationally.\n- In 2005, Kang Sung-yeon rose to fame by playing Jang Nok-su, Prince Yeonsan's concubine, in King and the Clown.\n- King and the Clown drew 12.3 admissions and at that time became the highest-grossing domestic film in Korean cinema history.\n- Tazza is a 2008 South Korean television series starring Jang Hyuk, Han Ye-seul, Kim Min-joon, Kang Sung-yeon, Son Hyun-joo, and Kim Kap-soo.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "300bfdd8-b7cc-5c18-adfd-b4458e85464f",
        "text": "Page: Kang Sung-yeon. Sentence: Then in 2005, Kang rose to fame when she played Prince Yeonsan's concubine Jang Nok-su in \"King and the Clown\", a period film that drew 12.3 admissions, making it (at the time) the highest-grossing domestic film in Korean cinema history.\nPage: King and the Clown. Sentence: It was released on 29 December 2005, runs for 119 minutes; and distributed domestically by Cinema Service and internationally by CJ Entertainment.\nPage: Tazza (TV series). Sentence: Tazza () is a 2008 South Korean television series starring Jang Hyuk, Han Ye-seul, Kim Min-joon, Kang Sung-yeon, Son Hyun-joo and Kim Kap-soo.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
